# eric-deployable.allow — the applications Eric (QA) may deploy to prod.
#
# WR-012 / ADR-0002. One bare application key per line (a repo-key of
# deployed-artifacts.tsv). `deploy <artifact>` refuses anything NOT listed here,
# and doctor.sh asserts this record contains NO out-of-bound target.
#
# THE BOUND IS THIS FILE. It rides on the manifest doctor.sh already self-checks,
# so it cannot silently drift; adding a target is a deliberate, recorded governance
# act (a commit here + operator install), never something the grant can do to itself.
#
# IN — the disposable, local-bare-repo applications. A total loss of either costs
# nothing; they are exactly PROCESS.md rule 2's shakedown targets.
slack-bridge
proxmox-dashboard

# OUT, and staying human-gated (Todd, on Steve's approval) — NEVER add these here:
#   agent-os          the substrate: routing, briefs, skills — governance, agent-denied,
#                     published via publish-substrate.sh, never deployed by an agent
#   ha-ops            the HA config mirror (PROCESS.md rule 2's named exclusion)
#   anything infra:true, or any Proxmox hypervisor
# Widening to any infra:true target is arguably its own ADR (ADR-0002 §2).
